admng-watchdog (0.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * No change in how the service works and no database migration.
  * Messages to users go through the message sanitizer shared with AD
    Manager, which now keeps Word's paragraph spacing hints
    mso-margin-top-alt and mso-margin-bottom-alt (one length or auto; inert
    in browsers, honoured by classic Outlook) and still drops every other
    mso-* property.
  * Rebuilt for AD Manager 0.7.0: Korespondencja (messages through classic
    Outlook) and the mailbox owner queries are AD Manager features that do
    not use the service.

 -- AD_MNG contributors <admng-watchdog@contoso.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0000

admng-watchdog (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Inline images in messages to users (AdMng 0.6.0, contract v2):
    POST /api/v1/user-messages accepts inlineImages (PNG, JPEG or GIF
    checked by content, at most 4096 x 4096 px, 10 images, 1 MiB each and
    2 MiB together, Content-ID derived from the SHA-256 of the bytes, every
    image referenced by the HTML); metadata is stripped and the images are
    sent as inline parts of multipart/related through the MIME builder
    shared with AD Manager. GET /api/v1/user-messages/status reports the
    inlineImages capability and the limits.
  * New settings userMessages.allowInlineImages (default on, off = 400
    imagesDisabled) and userMessages.maxStoredImageMb (default 256, range
    16-4096): images held in the outbox (unsent and given-up messages) are
    capped, over the cap 429 imageStorageFull with Retry-After 1 h;
    messages without images are not affected. Images live only in the
    outbox payload, are deleted once sent (a given-up message keeps them
    until the outbox retention, 90 days by default) and never reach the
    audit, the delivery log or the diagnostic log. Migration 0007 adds
    outbox.image_bytes. AD Manager 0.6.0 does not edit the two settings
    yet; they are changed through PUT /api/v1/config.
  * POST /api/v1/user-messages alone accepts a request body of up to 6 MiB
    (every other route keeps 1 MB); the HTML body limit is 400,000
    characters (was 100,000). The HTML is checked by the message sanitizer
    shared with AD Manager (AngleSharp) and the sanitized document is sent;
    a message without images is refused only for what 0.4.0 refused and for
    nesting deeper than 256 levels, so AD Manager 0.4.0 and 0.5.0 keep
    working.
  * New delivery hint smtp.messageTooLarge for 5.3.4, 5.2.3 and a bare 552.
  * The remaining GPO content parsers (security template, audit.csv,
    Registry.pol, preferences, scripts, comments, GPT.INI), the setting
    model and the secret rules moved to AdMng.Core (shared with AD
    Manager's Group Policy views); no change of the service's behaviour.

 -- AD_MNG contributors <admng-watchdog@contoso.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000

admng-watchdog (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * AdMng 0.5.0: no functional change of the service. The privileged group
